# Security-owned paths — copy into a consumer repo as .github/CODEOWNERS
#
# WHY THIS MATTERS
#
# `gate_mode: log-only` makes the gate genuinely non-blocking, including for
# report-integrity failures. Caller workflows are app-team-owned and edited by
# ordinary pull request, so without this file a one-line change turns a red
# required check green, reviewed by whoever normally reviews that repo's code.
# That is an unreviewed path to bypassing the repo's own security gate.
#
# THIS FILE ALONE ENFORCES NOTHING. CODEOWNERS is advisory until branch
# protection on the default branch enables "Require review from Code Owners"
# with at least one required approval. See docs/onboarding.md § 1.4 and § 1.6.
#
# Own these with a TEAM, not an individual, so review does not depend on one
# person being available.

# Everything CI executes, including the framework ref and the gate mode.
/.github/workflows/          @your-org/security-engineering
/.github/CODEOWNERS          @your-org/security-engineering

# ssd-onboard's source of truth: gate mode, scan scope, framework ref, and every
# identifier the generated workflows use.
/.ssd/                       @your-org/security-engineering

# Scanner configuration. Each of these can narrow a scan without touching a
# workflow: a .semgrepignore line removes code from SAST, a .gitleaks.toml
# without `[extend] useDefault = true` replaces every built-in secret rule, and
# an exclude line hides paths from TruffleHog.
/.semgrepignore              @your-org/security-engineering
/.gitleaks.toml              @your-org/security-engineering
/.trufflehog-exclude-paths.txt @your-org/security-engineering

# The accepted-findings baseline. Whoever can rewrite this can accept any
# finding permanently and silently.
/security/baseline/          @your-org/security-engineering

# Deliberate, owned, expiring exceptions.
/security/exemptions.json    @your-org/security-engineering

# Only if this repo overrides the framework's default policy.
/security/policy.yaml        @your-org/security-engineering
